                // Positional arg before help? But help ignores extra positional? We saw --help extra => still help (ignores extra). So positional before help not error? But extra after --help is ignored. What about positional before help? Example "extra --help"? We didn't test. But likely if extra appears before help, it would be considered file arg and help would still print? Need to check.
                // For now, ignore.
            }
            i += 1;
        }
